1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,780
Well, hello, Canvas Community Church, and welcome to the last Sunday of the year here.

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:13,960
It has been our tradition to not have any in-person gatherings on the last Sunday of the year,

3
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:20,880
and historically we have elected to pre-record a service to give our staff and all of our incredible volunteers

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:25,500
an intentional rest at the end of a long and busy year.

5
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:30,200
We're going to be talking about Sabbath here in a few weeks at the church,

6
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,980
and just a reminder that God invites us to rest in His presence

7
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:42,880
and that a relationship with God is not rooted in what we do for Him, but what we do with Him.

8
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:49,440
And typically we record a pretty standard service with a few worship songs and a short devotional message.

9
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:55,200
However, this year I have really been impacted by some guided prayer meditations

10
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:02,040
from an app called Lectio 365, put together by an organization called 24-7 Prayer.

11
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:08,860
Love for you to check that out and find if it is beneficial to you in your spiritual journey at all.

12
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:14,300
They have three kind of prayer meditations a day, a morning, a midday, and an evening.

13
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:23,000
And so I decided that I would attempt to write out a guided prayer meditation for us using this Lectio format.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,540
I think it is a helpful reminder to us that spiritual formation is not just an isolated activity in the brain,

15
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,680
but it includes our whole person.

16
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:41,080
And we actually did a foundational sermon series on this a while back called Spiritual Stations,

17
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:46,440
just about how we as different people worship and connect with God in different ways.

18
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:49,660
And Lectio and prayer meditation was one of those ways.

19
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:57,900
And so if you missed that series or you want to refresh, I will post a link to that in the comments just so you can check that out.

20
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:04,200
But just hopefully today becomes an opportunity for us to just sit in the presence of God,

21
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,980
our whole selves, bring our whole selves into prayer,

22
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:13,440
and ask the Holy Spirit to work through the prayers and the reading of Scripture and the meditation

23
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:20,440
to just draw us closer into His presence and conform us more into His image.

24
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:23,520
We decided not to record some worship songs.

25
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:32,460
And instead, I am going to put a slide on the screen with some songs that would pair well with our meditation this morning.

26
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:41,720
If you want to pause this video and go find your favorite recording of whatever your favorite song is that's listed on the screen,

27
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:50,100
or just a song that you feel will help prepare your heart or your family or your small group's heart for this time of prayer and meditation.

28
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,520
So feel free to do that.

29
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,980
If not, I'm going to go ahead and pray and we can get started.

30
00:02:56,520 --> 00:03:08,200
Father in heaven, we thank you for another year, another opportunity to, God, just experience you in new ways,

31
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:13,600
experience you in old ways, be challenged and convicted and encouraged.

32
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:19,060
And God, we just thank you for the gift of life, the gift of breath in our lungs.

33
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:25,480
And we just pray for this upcoming year, God, that we as a people of God would be led by the Spirit,

34
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:31,260
be conformed into the image of Jesus, embody the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven,

35
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:34,320
for your glory, for our good, for the good of our neighbor.

36
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,160
Amen.

37
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:47,980
Well, in 1925, Pope Pius XI added a service to the church calendar called Christ is King.

38
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:57,880
It was a response to rising nationalism, secularism, and the marginalization of Christ's authority and public discourse.

39
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:05,640
It is now celebrated by many streams of the church, and it is typically celebrated on the last Sunday of the church calendar

40
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:09,040
or the last Sunday before Advent begins.

41
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:13,780
However, since we don't strictly follow any liturgical calendar,

42
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:21,280
I thought the last Sunday of the calendar year would be a good opportunity for us to reflect on the kingship of Christ,

43
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:27,500
his cross-shaped kingdom of sacrificial and self-giving love,

44
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,620
his resurrection and ascension to the throne,

45
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:34,500
demonstrating his kingdom and his dominion over all creation,

46
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:39,800
and his eventual return, making visible his authority over all creation.

47
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:43,540
It's aimed at challenging our competing allegiances,

48
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:48,240
whether they be political, national, ideological, or personal.

49
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,120
So as we pray together today,

50
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:55,200
I invite each of us to consider our allegiances over the past year.

51
00:04:55,880 --> 00:05:01,200
In what areas of our lives did we allow Christ to function as King?

52
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:09,340
In what area of our lives have we given our ultimate allegiance to someone else or something else?

53
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:19,080
And how might the Holy Spirit be inviting us to bend the knee of surrender to the teachings and examples of Jesus in this coming year?

54
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:26,860
We will be using the pattern from Lectio Divina where they pause, reflect, ask, and yield.

55
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,900
P-R-A-Y.

56
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:35,440
And so, as we enter prayer now, we pause to be still.

57
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:39,620
Breathe slowly.

58
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:46,400
We recenter our scattered senses upon the indwelling presence of God.

59
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:53,340
Almighty and everlasting God,

60
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:58,380
whose will it is to restore all things in your well-beloved Son,

61
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:01,580
the King of kings and Lord of lords,

62
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:05,180
mercifully grant that peoples of the earth,

63
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:07,200
divided and enslaved by sin,

64
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:11,740
may be freed and brought together under his most gracious rule,

65
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:15,780
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit,

66
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:17,160
one God,

67
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,860
now and forever.

68
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:20,060
Amen.

69
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:28,060
We choose to rejoice today with this opening line from the Royal Psalm, Psalm 93.

70
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,380
The Lord reigns.

71
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:34,260
He is robed in majesty.

72
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:37,960
The Lord is robed in majesty and armed with strength.

73
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:41,740
Indeed, the world is established firm and secure.

74
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:45,500
Your throne was established long ago.

75
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:50,120
You are from all eternity.

76
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:53,440
In today's Scripture reading,

77
00:06:53,440 --> 00:07:00,000
we turn to a famous dialogue between Jesus and Pontius Pilate prior to his crucifixion.

78
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,700
Scripture reads,

79
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:07,340
Pilate then went back inside the palace,

80
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:09,660
summoned Jesus and asked him,

81
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,580
Are you the King of the Jews?

82
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:14,240
Is that your own idea?

83
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,080
Jesus asked.

84
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,800
Or did others talk to you about me?

85
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,300
Am I a Jew?

86
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,440
Pilate replied.

87
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:24,180
Your own people and chief priests handed you over to me.

88
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,620
What is it that you have done?

89
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:27,560
Jesus said,

90
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,420
My kingdom is not of this world.

91
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:30,680
If it were,

92
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:35,160
my servants would fight to prevent my arrest by the Jewish leaders.

93
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:38,220
But now my kingdom is from another place.

94
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,620
You are a king then,

95
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,320
said Pilate.

96
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,840
Jesus answered,

97
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:43,440
You say that I am a king.

98
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:44,460
In fact,

99
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:48,340
the reason I was born and came into this world is to testify to the truth.

100
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:51,760
Everyone on the side of truth listens to me.

101
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,180
What is truth?

102
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,700
Retorted Pilate.

103
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:57,080
With this,

104
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,800
he went out again to the Jews,

105
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,220
gathered there and said,

106
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,960
I find no basis for charge against him,

107
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:07,580
but it is your custom for me to release to you one prisoner at the time of the Passover.

108
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:10,520
Do you want me to release this King of the Jews?

109
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,900
They shouted back,

110
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,360
No, not him.

111
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,700
Give us Barabbas.

112
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:24,640
The secular politician missed the nature of Christ's kingdom,

113
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:31,020
and the religious Jews rejected the cross-shaped sacrificial nature of his kingdom.

114
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:48,220
In what ways might we miss the nature of God's kingdom or the cross-shaped sacrificial nature of his kingdom.

115
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,720
Sovereign Lord and King of the universe,

116
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:59,060
we acknowledge our propensity to misunderstand the nature of your kingdom and to give our allegiance to other things.

117
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:04,720
Please awaken our heart to see this rebellion and rejection when it happens.

118
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:09,460
Give us the strength to believe that your ways are better than our ways,

119
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:11,840
that your thoughts are better than our thoughts,

120
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:19,160
and help us this year to surrender wholeheartedly to your kingdom with a glad and sincere heart.

121
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:30,540
I invite you to think now of someone in your life who has rejected God's kingdom for a lesser allegiance.

122
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:37,700
Spend time now asking God to awaken their hearts to his kingdom in this coming year.

123
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:46,800
Pray that God might use you as an ambassador to this person or persons in a way that leads to their salvation.

124
00:09:46,960 --> 00:10:05,380
Father in heaven, may your kingdom come and your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

125
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:12,000
As we return to the passage in John,

126
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:17,220
we listen for the Holy Spirit to speak a specific word of challenge or encouragement to us.

127
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:26,140
What word or phrase might God be inviting us to meditate on from this passage in the coming hours or days?

128
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:32,880
Pilate then went back inside the palace, summoned Jesus and asked him,

129
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,700
Are you king of the Jews?

130
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:39,780
Is that your own idea, Jesus asked, or did others talk to you about me?

131
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,280
Am I a Jew?

132
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,080
Pilate replied.

133
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:45,380
Your own people and chief priests handed you over to me.

134
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,100
What is it you have done?

135
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:49,400
Jesus said,

136
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:51,380
My kingdom is not of this world.

137
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:55,580
If it were, my servants would fight to prevent my arrest by the Jewish leaders.

138
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:57,960
But now my kingdom is from another place.

139
00:10:57,960 --> 00:11:00,880
You are a king then, said Pilate.

140
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,320
Jesus answered,

141
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,600
You say that I am king.

142
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:08,120
In fact, the reason I was born and came into this world is to testify to the truth.

143
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:11,140
Everyone on the side of truth listens to me.

144
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,140
What is truth?

145
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,040
Retorted Pilate.

146
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,660
With this, he went out again to the Jews,

147
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,120
gathered there and said,

148
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:20,520
I find no basis for a charge against him.

149
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:25,260
But it is your custom for me to release to you one prisoner at the time of Passover.

150
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:28,000
Do you want me to release the king of the Jews?

151
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,500
They shouted back,

152
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,700
No, not him.

153
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,600
Give us Barabbas.

154
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:41,460
And now,

155
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:46,120
as we prepare to take this time of prayer into our coming day,

156
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,600
the Lord who loves us,

157
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:53,100
assures us of this current spiritual reality in the book of Revelation.

158
00:11:53,100 --> 00:12:12,880
Father, help me to live this day to the full, being true to you in every way.

159
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:18,520
Jesus, help me to give myself away to others, being kind to everyone I need.

160
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:21,800
Spirit, help me to love the lost,

161
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:27,060
proclaiming Christ the King in all I do and say.

162
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,440
Amen.
